{
  // `lib` is ES2024 and nothing else, and `types` is empty — the same closure
  // packages/domain uses, for the same reason and one more.
  //
  // The reason it shares: docs/architecture.md requires that "no Web Bluetooth
  // type escapes above the transport boundary", and this package *is* above the
  // transport boundary. Without the DOM lib, `navigator`, `BluetoothDevice` and
  // `BluetoothRemoteGATTCharacteristic` are compile errors here rather than
  // review findings; with `types: []`, so are `process` and `Buffer`.
  //
  // The reason it is stricter than it looks: the whole point of #39 is that the
  // same interfaces are implemented by Web Bluetooth (#40), and later by
  // CoreBluetooth and the Android BLE APIs (#15). An interface that can name a
  // browser type has already chosen one of the three.
  //
  // ⚠️ This closure is conditional. `types: []` suppresses the automatic @types
  // lookup; it does *not* stop a `/// <reference types="node" />` inside a
  // `.d.ts` that a file in this program imports. That is why `vitest.config.ts`
  // imports nothing — see the comment at the top of it — and why
  // eslint.config.js keeps a denylist that does not depend on this holding.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2024"],
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "vitest.config.ts"]
}
